    "body": "This looks like exactly one meaningful change - wrapping it in a DOMContentLoaded listener rather than just executing immediately. I expect that this is inserted at the end of the document currently, tho, so the two are essentially equivalent.\r\n\r\nThe rest of this is just naive respellings - switching a chain of `.then()`s into an async function that's then invoked, or changing `function` declarations into const arrow functions. That might actually be a breaking change, since those functions are captured by earlier functions; I forget if TDZ makes that broken or not.\r\n\r\nOther than those light syntactic changes, there is zero changed functionality.",
